WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.688
Pinocchio was quite worried about his nose.

2
00:00:03.689 --> 00:00:07.683
He looked so silly that the Blue Fairy began to laugh.

3
00:00:07.684 --> 00:00:11.349
"Why are you laughing?" cried Pinocchio.

4
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:15.290
"I am laughing at your lies," said the fairy.

5
00:00:15.291 --> 00:00:17.988
"It's easy to tell when you are lying.

6
00:00:17.989 --> 00:00:22.065
Your nose grows with every lie you tell."

7
00:00:22.066 --> 00:00:25.497
Ashamed, Pinocchio turned bright red.

8
00:00:25.498 --> 00:00:29.953
"I'm sorry," said Pinocchio.

9
00:00:29.954 --> 00:00:33.858
"I took the money from the marionette master.

10
00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:38.251
My father didn't know I went to the theater."

11
00:00:38.252 --> 00:00:42.586
"Do you promise to be a good boy and obey your father?"

12
00:00:42.587 --> 00:00:45.171
she asked before waving her wand.

13
00:00:45.172 --> 00:00:49.231
"Yes, I promise!" Pinocchio said.

14
00:00:49.232 --> 00:00:53.423
The Blue Fairy waved her wand, and a woodpecker appeared.

15
00:00:53.424 --> 00:00:58.884
It pecked his nose down to size.

16
00:00:58.885 --> 00:01:03.192
Then, the jail bars disappeared and Pinocchio climbed free.

17
00:01:03.193 --> 00:01:08.165
"This is the road that leads home," said the Blue Fairy, pointing.

18
00:01:08.166 --> 00:01:13.887
"If you stay on this road, you will reach Geppetto’s home by nightfall.

19
00:01:13.888 --> 00:01:17.620
Remember your promise to be a good boy, Pinocchio!"

20
00:01:17.621 --> 00:01:21.302
she called, and she flew away.

21
00:01:21.303 --> 00:01:26.104
"Oh, what an awful thing it is to disobey our parents!

22
00:01:26.105 --> 00:01:30.347
From now on I will do whatever Geppetto asks,"

23
00:01:30.348 --> 00:01:34.906
Pinocchio said as he walked down the road.

24
00:01:34.907 --> 00:01:38.819
A few hours later, Pinocchio began to get hungry.

25
00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:43.438
He saw a nearby grapevine and decided to ask the owner for some grapes.

26
00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:47.140
As he crossed the field, he fell into a trap.

27
00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:53.090
"Oh no! Someone, help me!" Pinocchio cried.

28
00:01:53.091 --> 00:01:58.342
"Aha, I have caught you," said the farmer, who was hiding.

29
00:01:58.343 --> 00:02:03.187
"So, you are the one who has been stealing my chickens."

30
00:02:03.188 --> 00:02:07.124
"No, sir. I have not stolen any chickens.

31
00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:13.300
Please, I was going to ask for some grapes because I am very hungry."

32
00:02:13.301 --> 00:02:17.355
"Aha! You were going to steal my grapes!

33
00:02:17.356 --> 00:02:21.751
I’ll show you what we do with thieves!" he said.

34
00:02:21.752 --> 00:02:26.022
He pulled Pinocchio from the trap and took him home.

35
00:02:26.023 --> 00:02:30.759
When the farmer got home, he locked a chain around Pinocchio’s neck.

36
00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:34.848
"My guard dog died this morning," said the farmer.

37
00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:38.753
"So tonight you will be a dog and guard my chicken coop.

38
00:02:38.754 --> 00:02:42.819
Tomorrow, I will decide how to punish you."

39
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:49.136
Poor Pinocchio. He had tried to be a good boy, but the farmer didn’t believe him.

40
00:02:49.137 --> 00:02:52.184
He was so hungry that he became tired.

41
00:02:52.185 --> 00:02:56.326
So, he crawled into the doghouse and fell asleep.

42
00:02:56.327 --> 00:03:00.818
Many hours passed, and Pinocchio heard voices nearby.

43
00:03:00.819 --> 00:03:02.973
He looked outside the doghouse.

44
00:03:02.974 --> 00:03:04.811
It was already night!

45
00:03:04.812 --> 00:03:08.150
He saw four weasels next to the chicken coop.

46
00:03:08.151 --> 00:03:12.642
"Who are you?" Pinocchio asked. They stopped.

47
00:03:12.643 --> 00:03:16.547
"Well, who are you?" one of the weasels asked.

48
00:03:16.548 --> 00:03:19.432
"And, where is our friend Oscar?"

49
00:03:19.433 --> 00:03:24.055
Pinocchio guessed that Oscar was the dog who had died, so he said,

50
00:03:24.056 --> 00:03:26.399
"Oscar died this morning.

51
00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.528
I am the new guard dog.

52
00:03:28.529 --> 00:03:32.396
Who are you?" Pinocchio asked again.

53
00:03:32.397 --> 00:03:37.799
"We are the weasels, and we are here to get dinner," said one of the weasels.

54
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.053
"Oscar was our friend.

55
00:03:40.054 --> 00:03:45.045
I will make the same promise to you that I did to him.

56
00:03:45.046 --> 00:03:48.215
Every week, we would visit this coop.

57
00:03:48.216 --> 00:03:50.768
Oscar promised not to bark.

58
00:03:50.769 --> 00:03:56.194
So we would give one chicken to Oscar and take seven home for dinner.

59
00:03:56.195 --> 00:04:02.629
If you pretend to sleep, we will leave one chicken for you too."

60
00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:06.912
Before Pinocchio answered, the weasels snuck into the chicken coop.

61
00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:11.293
BAM! Pinocchio locked the door behind them and began to bark.

62
00:04:11.294 --> 00:04:15.416
"Woof, woof, woof!" he cried.

63
00:04:15.417 --> 00:04:19.689
The farmer ran down and found the weasels in the chicken coop.

64
00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.527
"Well done!" he said to Pinocchio.

65
00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:26.114
"You have caught the chicken thieves!

66
00:04:26.115 --> 00:04:29.688
Oscar must have been too old to hear them."

67
00:04:29.689 --> 00:04:33.821
Pinocchio didn’t say anything about Oscar’s promise to the weasels.

68
00:04:33.822 --> 00:04:35.297
He only nodded.

69
00:04:35.298 --> 00:04:40.909
"You have saved my chickens, so I will set you free," said the farmer.

70
00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:44.339
"But first, let me make you breakfast."

71
00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:51.355
Pinocchio nodded again, this time, with a big smile.

